{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once","id":1174247,"title":"About Juggling Several Effects at once.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-08T05:20:33-08:00","id":1174247,"title":"About Juggling Several Effects at once.","content":"Hello. This is my first post and I hope I'm doing it right.<br /> My question is: does a effect cast by an allied mage counts as an effect for the purpose of the cumulative +1 on difficulty per two effects? Or just the spells cast by me on myself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23699,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","user":"avatarmagus","date":". 01-08-2018, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","name":"avatarmagus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T06:26:11-08:00","id":1174258,"title":"","content":"The cumulative penalty only applies to effects YOU are concentrating on. Multiple active effects that are lasting for their normal duration will not count as concentration (unless it's an effed like giving yourself telekinesis, which requires you to concentrate to move something with your mind).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T07:46:08-08:00","id":1174274,"title":"","content":"Indeed.<br /> Only effects the mage needs to actively concentrate on (delicate forces work/flight/telekinesis, mind control, etc.) apply to this.<br /> Also of note, another thing that falls under this is actively prolonging an effect past its duration - even if you only manage to make an effect last for a turn or hour or whatever, you can prolong it by actively focusing on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T07:52:44-08:00","id":1174276,"title":"","content":"According to M20 Core page 329:<br /> <br /> &quot;As an overall note, an Effect that has a Time-based trigger,<br /> one which has been locked into another Pattern, or one that<br /> has been cast but whose duration has not yet expired, does not<br /> count toward that total. If Lee Ann enchants a guy, and if \u2013<br /> thanks to the number of successes rolled \u2013 that enchantment<br /> lasts for a week after they part company, then Lee Ann does<br /> not have to concentrate on the Effect in order to keep it going.<br /> If she wishes to keep the Effect in motion, however, then it<br /> counts against the number of Effects that character can employ<br /> at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> I became confused by the last line of this entry (especially the part where it says &quot;If she wishes to keep the Effect in motion...&quot;).<br /> <br /> It will help if anyone could give me some examples of effects that count as &quot;juggling several effects at once&quot; and some that doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","name":"avatarmagus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T08:08:45-08:00","id":1174281,"title":"","content":"Basically, if you cast an effect that could last for a week, but you only want it to go for a few moments, that\u2019s fine, the effect drops after you leave and no extra juggling is required.<br /> <br /> It only counts towards the difficulty if you chose to keep it up for the week. If you do, then that difficulty increase will stay with you for the entire week, or up until you dismiss the effect, whichever comes first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T08:15:22-08:00","id":1174283,"title":"","content":"Let's suppose that I cast two effects that last for a day, but I have 2 effects casted by another mage on me that last for a story, is there any penalty for my character in this case (assume that I cast effects like increasing traits and soak aggravated damage)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23699,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","user":"avatarmagus","date":". 01-08-2018, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","name":"avatarmagus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T15:25:19-08:00","id":1174371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>avatarmagus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174283#post1174283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's suppose that I cast two effects that last for a day, but I have 2 effects casted by another mage on me that last for a story, is there any penalty for my character in this case (assume that I cast effects like increasing traits and soak aggravated damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Unless they are doing some kind of Prime/Entropy Mind/Spirit magic, or have Primium, no one can magically impose penalties on to you (nephandi and their weird spheres permitting).<br /> <br /> The reason multiple effects is difficult is because each effect requires the concentration of the caster to maintain.<br /> <br /> The more effects they have going, the more distracted they will be, making it difficult to focus. Think of it like trying to sing your favourite song while trying to remember a phone number you only just saw. Now do all that while making a sandwich. It gets difficult. So too will magic is you keep distracting yourself with loads of ongoing effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 01-08-2018, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T16:32:28-08:00","id":1174385,"title":"","content":"Thanks to all for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23699-avatarmagus","name":"avatarmagus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-08T23:22:55-08:00","id":1174475,"title":"","content":"@Saiku, I disagree with your interpretation of the quote that avatarmagus cited in Comment #4--assuming I am interpreting your interpretation correctly. To me it seems to be stating that the concentration penalty only applies if you keep an Effect going longer than you should be able to based on the number of duration successes. This means that the rule is not actually a hindrance, but rather a whole other option for keeping an Effect going if you can't get as many duration successes as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 01-09-2018, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T01:49:22-08:00","id":1174499,"title":"","content":"@faradn<br /> You\u2019re right, that is not at all how I interpret it.<br /> For every effect active, the penalty applies.<br /> If you have 3 effects that last for a scene, then the penalty applies until the next scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T03:25:49-08:00","id":1174510,"title":"","content":"I also agree with Faradn's interpretation, since the text explicitely states:<br /> <br /> &quot;As an overall note, an Effect that has a <b>Time-based trigger</b>,<br /> one which has been <b>locked into another Pattern</b>, or one that<br /> has been cast <b>but whose duration has not yet expired</b>, does <b>not</b><br /> count toward that total.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note the bold 'But whose duration has not yet expired'. Especially the 'not yet expired'.<br /> It implies two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Effects that require no active interaction by the mage (i.e. pattern-locked, time based etc.) and that have <i>not yet expired</i> do not count towards the total.<br /> 2) The 'not yet expired' implies that once they <b>do</b> expire, there is the option to keep them going - at the expense of making the effect, no matter its simplicity or nature, count towards the limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-09-2018, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T08:40:38-08:00","id":1174560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174510#post1174510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree with Faradn's interpretation, since the text explicitely states:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;As an overall note, an Effect that has a <b>Time-based trigger</b>,<br /> one which has been <b>locked into another Pattern</b>, or one that<br /> has been cast <b>but whose duration has not yet expired</b>, does <b>not</b><br /> count toward that total.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Note the bold 'But whose duration has not yet expired'. Especially the 'not yet expired'.<br /> It implies two things:<br /> <br /> 1) Effects that require no active interaction by the mage (i.e. pattern-locked, time based etc.) and that have <i>not yet expired</i> do not count towards the total.<br /> 2) The 'not yet expired' implies that once they <b>do</b> expire, there is the option to keep them going - at the expense of making the effect, no matter its simplicity or nature, count towards the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this exception only applies to locked in effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T17:24:15-08:00","id":1174710,"title":"","content":"Basically the only effects that count against the caster are those that require active manipulation during their duration. Weather control, mind control, personal force fields (this one is touchy but it's how we rule for our games), telekinesis, etc. Additionally any effect that has it's duration extended beyond that which was rolled during the arete roll. Nothing else.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly every active effect counted against a caster in Revised, so this is a big change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T18:06:48-08:00","id":1174720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174710#post1174710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically the only effects that count against the caster are those that require active manipulation during their duration. Weather control, mind control, personal force fields (this one is touchy but it's how we rule for our games), telekinesis, etc. Additionally any effect that has it's duration extended beyond that which was rolled during the arete roll. Nothing else.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly every active effect counted against a caster in Revised, so this is a big change.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably why I interpret it that way. I never really left revised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T21:03:13-08:00","id":1174763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174720#post1174720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably why I interpret it that way. I never really left revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had always understood it that way too, but I think I like this way better. Since successes are so hard to come by, I'm eager for opportunities to reduce success thresholds.<br /> <br /> It does raise another issue though. If meeting the success threshold means an Effect is essentially happening on its own, what if you want to end it early? Would you have to use countermagic on your own spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T03:41:37-08:00","id":1174822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174763#post1174763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does raise another issue though. If meeting the success threshold means an Effect is essentially happening on its own, what if you want to end it early? Would you have to use countermagic on your own spell?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, no. A Mage can always drop their own running effects, no matter the type - as long as *they* were the source of the Arete roll, basically.<br /> <br /> A Wonder that uses its own Arete dice though...that might actually be a different matter! If the Wonder has no theme-ish mechanism for dropping its effect before end of duration, I can actually see the Mage needing to unweave the effect that the Wonder created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:28:52-08:00","id":1174847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174822#post1174822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, no. A Mage can always drop their own running effects, no matter the type - as long as *they* were the source of the Arete roll, basically.<br /> <br /> A Wonder that uses its own Arete dice though...that might actually be a different matter! If the Wonder has no theme-ish mechanism for dropping its effect before end of duration, I can actually see the Mage needing to unweave the effect that the Wonder created.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could agree with that from a rule standpoint (and a comedic standpoint as well). For a serious game and to avoid needless issues I would probably allow it in most circumstances though.<br /> <br /> A disgruntal Fetish on the other hand could be problamatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:51:35-08:00","id":1174857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1174847#post1174847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could agree with that from a rule standpoint (and a comedic standpoint as well). For a serious game and to avoid needless issues I would probably allow it in most circumstances though.<br /> <br /> A disgruntal Fetish on the other hand could be problamatic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I could imagine a wonder with a static stubborn or pedantic resonance being quite unwilling to allow the mage to prematurely shut off its effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T20:43:35-08:00","id":1185474,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've given it more thought and I think I disagree with the book. Without restraints like this, duration Effects can be really OP. With enough successes in a ritual, you could ward bullets for the entire Chronicle, and have footsteps that make no sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T20:57:27-08:00","id":1185476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1185474#post1185474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've given it more thought and I think I disagree with the book. Without restraints like this, duration Effects can be really OP. With enough successes in a ritual, you could ward bullets for the entire Chronicle, and have footsteps that make no sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T22:35:26-08:00","id":1185495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1174247-about-juggling-several-effects-at-once?p=1185474#post1185474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've given it more thought and I think I disagree with the book. Without restraints like this, duration Effects can be really OP. With enough successes in a ritual, you could ward bullets for the entire Chronicle, and have footsteps that make no sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>The #1 deterrent against this kind of thing is quite simple:<br /> Magick-wise, the more and the stronger effects you got running, the more you are a beacon for anyone and anything that can sense Magick in the first place. Awareness rolls, Prime 1, the other level 1 spheres, etc.<br /> So while it's probably not even that uncommon for some mages to have a subtle effect running at any time, the more you pile on, the higher the chances for nightfolks and Mage factions antagonistic to you to spot you from afar. Especially certain Mage factions that oh so love keeping an eye on anything magickal and abnormal...<br /> And there is always the option to introduce exotic unknowns (or should I say, stranger things?) that get attracted to that kind of thing like fireflies.<br /> <br /> The #2 deterrent which is kind of optional is retroactive paradox.<br /> While M20 states that paradox is usually not retroactive (and I personally like that fact), it's always an option for the ST if you want a more low-key magick campaign.<br /> Have the mage with the silent footsteps suddenly be hit by non-witness paradox if they just keep on vainly strutting across things that, by all means and purposes should be rustling and clattering and crunching beneath their feet. If anything, that mage suddenly has to be careful where they thread, and wether they put on a sneaky act doing so or not, while the hail of stopped mid-air bullets becomes a quick trip to backlash town.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think both those options, especially the first, are better and more clever to use than limiting the duration and/or simultaneous effects logic in M20, as it meshes well with the tropes of long-term curses and blessings, enchanted items, traps in Sanctums and olde mysterious ruins, etc..at least while the Mage is alive. Else you need Wonders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-13-2018, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}